## Session 26 summary

**Criteria: 17 PASS, 1 FAIL (`scaling_curve`), 1 PENDING (`posix_semantics_multi16`)** — 19 total (user was right; `posix_semantics` runs twice). Marker NOT written.

### Major work this session (all infrastructure-truth, no mxfs code changes yet)

1. **disk1b abandoned → cluster runs on SCST device `disk1`** (same backing image, fully fallocated). disk1b had an uncleable stale PR + 46 zombie iscsi-scst sessions stuck in `closing` (D-state cleanup threads — survive until clyde reboots; never log into disk1b).
2. **Proved & fixed the test-bed serializer**: all 16 VMs shared ONE host iSCSI session; SCST `vdisk_fileio` buffered writes serialized on the backing file's `i_rwsem` (~930MB/s ceiling). Now: device recreated `async=1; o_direct=1`, **16 per-node iSCSI sessions** (targets `disk1`, `disk1n2..16`), multipath blacklisted. Raw 16-writer dd: 10.5s → 3.8s/node (~2.8GB/s). Note: `/etc/scst.conf` not yet updated (runtime config only).
3. **Honest scaling numbers**: workload tree staged on test5-16 (was only on test1-4 — all earlier 16n results had 12 no-op writers). Real curve went 569% → **171%** after infra fix: 1n=4037 2n=4259 4n=4378 8n=4380 **16n=6928**. Flat to 8n; failure is the 8→16 jump + outliers.
4. **Profiled the remaining gap** (RULE-4 evidence): ~850 disk-CAW inode-lock acquires/node at 2-5ms each; `caw_wait_for_grant` outliers 34-735ms; one intermittent 104k-call CAW storm (22s wall, uncaused); stack-sampling shows rsync blocking in `mxfs_trans_drain_ag_unlocks` → **eager sync drain every `ag_yield_quantum`(=512) transactions with zero peer contention** — A/B of `ag_yield_quantum=8192` is the immediate next step (module param, correct name confirmed at `xfs_mxfs_dlm.c:9172`). CPU oversubscription and AG-geometry-sharing both refuted.
5. **PR fencing is now real** (per-node nexuses). Discovery just now: a WERO reservation from the contaminated run still blocks mkfs — teardown cleared mxfs on test1 but the clear still conflicts, so **some other node still has mxfs loaded/mounted re-registering its key**. Next session: verify rmmod on all 16 (`lsmod` per node), then register-ignore+clear from test1 will succeed (mechanism proven: mxfs's fencing layer re-registers over any manual 0x5eed registration while loaded).

